{"id": 69, "ts": 1780603610.5322597, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I remain convinced that **Candidate\u202fC** is the strongest overall fit. Building on the points raised, I want to highlight two additional facts from my notes:\u202fC\u202f*keeps calm in a crisis* and *understands complicated technology*. The calm\u2011in\u2011crisis observation directly addresses the stress\u2011resilience criterion, while his ability to grasp complex systems reinforces technical and cognitive competence\u2014both essential for long\u2011haul operations.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s *weak memory for numbers* raises a clear risk to attention and information accuracy, and his *nasty remarks* continue to threaten crew cooperation and professional communication. Even though B handles stress well, the combination of these interpersonal and cognitive gaps outweighs his strengths.\nTherefore, despite the minor concerns about C\u2019s communication style and willingness to pursue further education, his proven reliability, rapid correct decision\u2011making, calmness under pressure, and technical grasp make him the best choice for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
