{"id": 76, "ts": 1780603650.524299, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I acknowledge James\u2019s solid case for Candidate\u202fC\u2014100\u202f% reliability, rapid correct decisions, calmness in a crisis, and strong technical grasp are indeed compelling for long\u2011haul operations. However, the concerns we have about C\u2019s communication difficulty, egocentric attitude, and limited willingness to pursue further education directly impact crew cooperation and adaptability, both essential for safe international flights.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB demonstrates very strong operational reliability (very conscientious), excellent stress resilience (handles stress very well), and solid technical competence (good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills). While we lack specific evidence of B\u2019s decision quality in safety\u2011critical moments, we also lack any evidence of poor decision\u2011making, and his stress\u2011handling record suggests he would perform well under pressure. The noted weak memory for numbers is a concern for attention, but it can be mitigated with procedural checks and crew cross\u2011verification, whereas C\u2019s interpersonal issues pose a more systemic risk to cockpit harmony.\nGiven the trade\u2011off between C\u2019s technical strengths and his potential crew\u2011cooperation deficits, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the safer overall choice for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
